 "summary": "The general totally-real identification and its continuity come first and the Lagrangian identification specializes them; the sign, surface and sphere results are derived from one general-`d` Euler theorem, and its `d + 1`, `Type` and `\ud835\udcd8(\u211d, X)` restrictions come from the existing `evalFundamentalClass_eulerClass_eq_eulerChar` and `eulerClass_eq_of_fiberwise` API. No general induced-normal-orientation construction exists in Tau Ceti to reuse (grep finds only `stableNormalOrientation` and `diagonalNormalOrientation`), so defining `lagrangianNormalOrientation` through `J` is at the right level for this target.",
